{
  "version": 197,
  "released": "2026-08-23",
  "changelog": "v197: research-only. `system/research/go-deep.md` \u2014 evidence-driven dating sessions, the domain research behind a deliberate, artifact-assisted sitting in which a person works at their own chronology and leaves with homework for a living relative (lifehug/lifehug-platform: \"Go Deep \u2014 the archaeology session under the Timeline\"). It answers the owner's question \u2014 is this a known practice? \u2014 with: it is the DOMINANT practice in three separate fields that converge on nearly the same session shape from unrelated starting points. Survey methodology supplies the instrument (Belli's event history calendar: randomized PSID experiments show better retrospective quality over reference periods up to 30 years for about 10% more interview time, with the honest caveat that it OVERREPORTS some counts). Oral history supplies the ethics and conduct (consent, refusal, the etiquette of contradiction \u2014 attribute the challenge to the source, never to the person's memory \u2014 and Baylor's three-phase cycle that puts verification BETWEEN sittings, which is the discipline's own name for homework). Genealogy supplies the epistemology (the Genealogical Proof Standard, direct/indirect/negative evidence, and the research log, whose three properties the design copies exactly: planned alongside done, negative results explicit and visually distinct from not-yet-asked, and built to survive a pause). AMENDS chronology.md \u00a76 rung 5: behavior-coding of 165 PSID calendar interviews finds that INTERVIEWER parallel (cross-domain) probes are associated with POORER data quality while timing and duration probes \u2014 'when did that start, when did it stop, how long' \u2014 are associated with better; the instrument affording parallel retrieval and the interviewer forcing it are different acts. Two structural findings run through the whole review: the method is INTERVAL INTERSECTION rather than date estimation (an empty intersection is a finding, never something to average away), and the PRECISION HIERARCHY INVERTS what people expect \u2014 a photograph is the least precisely datable object in the box (decade at worst, a few years at best) while the unglamorous paper around it is exact to the day, so a session leads with what is NEAR the photo. Also recorded: the false-memory constraint (genuine photographs plus suggestive interviewing produced the highest rate then published \u2014 so a dig must never propose a date for confirmation), that the benefit of objects is REVIEW rather than the visual modality, school-year arithmetic with its cutoff table and its honest error rate (about one adult in five is off by a year through redshirting, retention or early entry), the residence spine, and the privacy line: reading a document aloud satisfies GDPR data-minimisation BY CONSTRUCTION where ingesting the image does not. THE LIVING SOURCE: 'interview the eldest first' turns out to be codified in exactly one place \u2014 US federal statute, which orders the Library of Congress to 'attempt to collect the first such recordings from the oldest veterans' \u2014 and is folk wisdom everywhere else, absent from both certifying bodies. Collaborative inhibition is NOT a threat to a targeted dating question (dyads, structured material, imposed order and people who know each other well are the minimum-inhibition corner of the meta-analysis's own moderators); it IS a threat to open reminiscing. Discrete, witnessed facts survive thirty years nearly intact while gradual ones drift later, so ask relatives about EVENTS, not processes. THE VALUE MATH, demonstrated by running the real v196 code over a synthetic vault: the top-two keystone list DOUBLE-COUNTS \u2014 one keystone's resolve set was a strict subset of the other's, so the second star's marginal gain was exactly zero and the pair covered 8 of 12 unknowns, while a greedy plan over the RESIDUAL graph covered 11 of 12 in two questions and surfaced the one unknown no anchor reaches at all. Proposed: greedy marginal cover (monotone submodular, so within (1-1/e) of optimal), ranked on continuous width reduction and never on a threshold count, kept inside the Simple Temporal Problem fragment where Floyd-Warshall is exact in O(n^3). NAMING is a first-class section surveying the actual terms of art across archaeology, chronology, oral tradition, genealogy, archival practice, ethnography and survey methodology: recommendation is 'Go Deep' as the VERB (the owner's own, and a Play control needs a verb) with 'a dig' as the NOUN, yielding dig plan and dig list; runner-up 'sounding' (the archaeological sondage, and 'to sound someone out' \u2014 the only candidate carrying two of the three senses); 'cross-dating' adopted as the name of the mechanic; 'ask now while you can' kept as a SENTENCE deployed once with the person named, never as a row label; and `witness` as the field naming the living person who was there. QUEUE.md gains a twelve-item Go Deep section led by the one source that most needs verifying (Vansina's floating gap). Nothing is implemented.",
